---
title: "Layout"
description: "Display, position, overflow, and stacking."
section: Utilities
sectionOrder: 3
order: 1
---

Where an element sits and how it clips. `--display` also carries the flex shorthands (`flex-col`, `inline-flex-row`) that set the direction with the display, so there is no separate direction utility.

`--anchor-name` and `--position-anchor` take states and breakpoints, so the anchor can move with interaction: put `--anchor-name--hover: --block` on every block of an editor, and a toolbar with `--position: absolute; --position-anchor: --block` follows the hovered one. `--position-area` places it: `--position-area: block-start span-inline-end` puts the toolbar above the block, aligned to its start. For finer placement write `anchor()` in plain CSS. The inset utilities take numbers and lengths only, so `--top: anchor(bottom)` computes to `0`.

